From 2f24b63a3f87dbe43239c4ba395db8338d7ebdee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timur Ravilov <93673987+t0b1kent@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 12:44:31 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] Darwin: arm hook and alias correctness when CLR code
 generation modules map

Arm HG1/HG2/HG3 and ALIAS once coreclr.dll or clrjit.dll maps, before the
existing image handler executes. No application profile is required.
The exact emergency switch MACRUNNER_FEX_ALIAS_AUTO=0 keeps the policy off.
Preallocate hook-depth TLS before hooks are active; publish one arm record
with module, guest PID, UTC and QPC. Pending early maps are retained.
Keep the JIT entry and validation machinery unchanged while unarmed.
Wine L0, diagnostic transport, VALIDATE1/WV1 and UnixLib ABI8 are unchanged.

Family: module notifications and guarded allocator/cache hook boundaries
Members: ARM64EC and WOW64 HandleImageMap; HG1/HG2/HG3 scopes and all existing
memory hooks; executable alias range lookup and NoTrap validation policy.
Trigger: named coreclr forwarder plus original alias-vp guest code.
Coverage: both PE architectures; exact case-insensitive module basenames;
early/late/concurrent one-shot publication; emergency off; existing hooks.
Regression: extracted policy 8/8; named alias target probes 8/8 plus flush
control PASS; native stand quick160/full500595, known1/651, new0.
Audit completed: yes. Field and timing are pending separate acceptance.
